    {
      "id": "shielded-night",
      "decision": "source-build",
      "inArtifactNormalizationScope": false,
      "reason": "Application code (a Compact contract plus its Vite/React dApp) with no reusable warehouse runtime artifact. Built from effectstream/shielded-night at an immutable full commit on the long-lived ledger-v9 branch, with the commit baked into both runtime images as /.shielded-night-commit and asserted by scripts/verify-source-pins.sh. The one EXTERNAL artifact its build fetches is the compactc 0.34.0 Linux musl release asset, SHA-256-pinned per architecture in images/shielded-night/Dockerfile: the contract is recompiled in-image and the build fails unless the output is byte-identical to the pinned tree's committed src/managed/, which is what makes the served prover keys provably the ones the on-chain verifier keys came from (project 00007, question Q3 -> owner decision A)."
    }
